msgid "Building Mission Planner with Visual Studio"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:8
#: 6fb93719fd81445aa83722d3cb80fbc1
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:10
#: 87add199af6b428da433503e2a42fc53
msgid "Mission Planner (MP) is an open source ground station developed in C# primarily for use on Windows/linux computers (although it can be run on Mac and Linux using mono). This is the most commonly used ground station as it provides the most complete functionality for vehicle setup as well as pre-flight mission planner, in-flight monitoring and post flight log file analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:17
#: 92bd73119f784877963ae70606d4deba
msgid "This page provides instructions on how you can build the Mission Planner software on your own machine using MS Visual Studio which may be useful if you wish to make changes for your own use or improvements for the community.  Building the mission planner may also help as a guide in case you plan to build your own custom ground station development."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:23
#: fd2d1c32d6e64270a2cb3d21dc0ab61e
msgid "Some warnings before you dive in:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:25
#: d62ef4b1422b430cae0e2d3c62dad963
msgid "Use your modified / complied version of Mission Planner at your own risk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:27
#: a48ec5aac4584d0a87c4670501ab7ccb
msgid "Mission Planner is a very complex including and making changes is not for the faint of heart. Here are the basic skills you will need to make reasonable progress with MP changes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:31
#: 9d7534f4dc8d4f5b9e47de8eb72e54c1
msgid "C# programming skills and experience (at least or C++ experience)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:32
#: e2b8e1f3745b44c6bac4ae10584be36f
msgid "Experience with Microsoft Visual Studio (VS) development environment. MP is not the application to begin learning VS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:34
#: 1c9386728fdb4c3e95c2e67cb696f158
msgid "Experience using Windows API  (Application programming Interface)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:35
#: fff5622c8b9b4863afb2da9ed53b9b50
msgid "Including understanding of streams, processes, threads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:37
#: 5fe35d2824da4a4ab780112fce752134
msgid "Support for Visual Studio, programming in C# and Windows API may not be forthcoming from the DIY Drones community. You will need to get that support from other sources."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:42
#: 89e8cb892dd746beadb6ee9c39276812
msgid "System Requirements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:44
#: ecb039859a5547909108768a14db8670
msgid "Here is what you will need."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:46
#: 3835bd4b3ef5419580b90eea2e59fde4
msgid "Windows 10 or later (Windows 7 and older versions are not compatible)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:47
#: c6943c34afb34fff9c716d8848c21e54
msgid "Sufficient disk space (around 20GB for VS installation), memory, processor power to comfortably run Visual Studio."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:49
#: 3f897e2ab40845e7b726779cf76949e0
msgid "An Internet connection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:50
#: 7e713ac8a3524526b5062afdd01c328c
msgid "Visual Studio (**NOT VSCode**), at least version 2022. The Community Edition suffices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:53
#: 2bd95795f209496caac51032c870ba9a
msgid "Install Visual Studio"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:55
#: 32868f061902466f8d2287a76fb767d5
msgid "Begin by installing Microsoft Visual Studio and configuring it for your Windows system. Follow these steps:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:57
#: 2489673114ff48469ece7f626f410930
msgid "Download Visual Studio: Visit the `Microsoft Visual Studio download page <https://visualstudio.microsoft.com/downloads/>`__ and download the Community Edition by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:59
#: 37464ae45c3d4e56a52acdcb4b49352d
msgid "Customize Installation: Visual Studio is a comprehensive suite with built-in Git support, but it can be overwhelming due to its complexity. To streamline the installation process, consider these steps: - Access \"More\" in the Visual Studio installer. - Choose \"Import configuration.\" - Import the provided configuration file: `vs2022.vsconfig <https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ArduPilot/MissionPlanner/master/vs2022.vsconfig>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:64
#: 96d12530b0d14938a11aa3b779c4fcb8
msgid "By following these instructions, you will have the necessary components installed and ready for Mission Planner development."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:67
#: fd52d6c00b31487d8d8e3dfc9305aa14
msgid "VSCode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:69
#: b3cd26c0d31a4757bcee29d128d934eb
msgid "While Visual Studio Code with the C# plugin can parse the code, please note that it **cannot build** Mission Planner at this time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:73
#: 2c7ed13ff591457ab0a676b2fe2dfd1b
msgid "After your VS installation is complete:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:75
#: e64734ac57034710b1569451a6990a51
msgid "You should be able to use Git from the IDE. Clone `Mission Planner source code <https://github.com/ArduPilot/MissionPlanner.git>`__ to get the full code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:78
#: 491d1f6c7d5944ea986ed20070e3fd40
msgid "Building the MissionPlanner"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:80
#: 0ae2b86a15f84ce0a1a403fb31c66d15
msgid "To build the code, follow these steps:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:82
#: bae135988f264af1b49baf413cfa09f2
msgid "Open `MissionPlanner.sln` file with Visual Studio"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:83
#: 84968916baaa4a789dc46919592a5649
msgid "From the \"Build\" menu, select \"Build MissionPlanner\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:86
#: c3ac989f4d7d4adaa6008aa601a6d1f6
msgid "By default, Visual Studio will compile all projects and their dependencies as part of a build process."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:89
#: bd11f70e777a493a8cfb23b90a22b8df
msgid "Non Windows building"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:91
#: ea8c7c58497b4a0599f8bab45b7aa54a
msgid "Building Mission Planner on other systems isn't support currently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:95
#: 16ebdae8b40a4d9e8c3c5d79f24912b7
msgid "Building the SimpleExample"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:100
#: 535336869ae7405296fdde1685cb74ab
msgid "The \"SimpleExample\" solution is available as a near minimal application to demonstrate how a C# program can connect to a vehicle and cause it to arm or disarm. This example has many fewer dependencies than the full Mission Planner and is simpler to build and understand."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:105
#: 01ec0195573f4360855f91e1c7f063e5
msgid "Open the solution from Visual Studio by selecting File >> Open >> Project/Solution, and in the MissionPlanner code directory select ExtLibs / SimpleExample.sln ( close the MissionPlanner solution first if you have that open )"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:109
#: 9c6986cb0ec24001b85584f102b26ba1
msgid "Ensure the program can be build successfully by selecting Build >> Build Solution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:112
#: 2bbfa795adf149b3933fbb227c68be3f
msgid "After first checking that you can connect to your flight controller and arm it with the regular mission planner, disconnect the regular Mission Planner and then press \"Start\" to run the application in debug mode. When the \"Form1\" pops up, select the COM port, the baud rate (probably 115200) and press Connect.  If it successfully connects, press Arm/Disarm to attempt to arm the vehicle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:119
#: ecf19140e7174186b4e816311c4ee912
msgid "there is no error checking in the application if it fails to connect it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:124
#: 8c28f38d0e164107b3a308e52a92e466
msgid "Following instructions are deprecated and were only kept for example. There are probably not working and need update."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:128
#: a30668ecef0447fe8de4fa7eed811a0b
msgid "Editing and Debugging Mission Planner (and Other Tips)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:130
#: 8e0ba7df6c2741c781a992e7a27782fd
msgid "Editing and debugging details are beyond the scope of this Wiki. Debugging may result in some warnings. You should learn what they mean and take the necessary steps to resolve them if that is the case. Here is a simple debugging example to get you started."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:135
#: 023f0ed1ff804ffebbddf494c04568b0
msgid "Do not (yet) connect your AutoPilot Hardware ( CubeOrange, etc. ) to the compiled version of MP.  You must  first copy some .xml files to the bin/debug folder. See details below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:138
#: 95bb07867c0f4b0ba2ca23b1517af59e
msgid "First be sure VS is configured for debug (versus release) Set this in the top menu tools area or the configuration manager."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:140
#: 5712ff01812748c3b649efa61cc07fb8
msgid "Select menu DEBUG, Start Debugging.   (Or, press F5).  Mission Planner should run as you normally see it.  However, some important configuration files are missing so connection to the AutoPilot Hardware ( eg CubeOrange, etc ) is not recommended at this time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:145
#: f949c13e32ed4d58b8b03a75f48cdfdb
msgid "If after \"Start Debugging\" the program loading hangs in the splash screen and you see this message:  \"Managed Debugging Assistant 'LoaderLock' has detected a problem ...... \"'  and/or the debugger has paused at the line  Application.Run(new MainV2()); in ArduPilotMega.Program then do this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:151
#: b6e2030ebd564abda1435c436a788101
msgid "Select [Debug],  [Exceptions].   Expand the [Managed Debugging Assistants].  Uncheck the 'Loader Lock' check box"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:154
#: 94782bf1edd144ea9e022e5bd5ea9713
msgid "Close MP. (Or, select menu DEBUG, Stop Debugging in VS)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:155
#: b9ac8731dda4406298af5fd333da9a20
msgid "Next you can try setting a break point."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:157
#: ea4e7877ce4e49de827d8a16ead2537a
msgid "Expand the MissionPlanner project in the VS Solution Explorer so you see the objects included."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:159
#: 7697c45ef7fd4cfda9219d527de1e6ca
msgid "Scroll down to MainV2.cs, right click that object and select View Code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:161
#: edd5cb3360794bcca322e653f2c69181
msgid "In the code window for MainV2.cs, scroll down to the line \"public MainV2\" then to one of the first code lines after that ( currently it is a log.Info(\"...\"); line ) ."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:163
#: b7ef2f71547944a0b7c7cb5498798e09
msgid "Click in front of that line (In the dark gray bar on the left) to set a break point  (red circle)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:165
#: 710bbadba28f4eee980ce9341382f8fb
msgid "Start Debugging  (press F5)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:166
#: 4fc84aae93f34e07a23bb72ded7bc86e
msgid "You will see the normal MP start up windows up to the Splash window but then it will stop running.  You have hit the break point. Visual Studio will show the code and the break point will be highlighted. Note that you cannot move the splash screen so you may need to relocate the VS window to see the break point."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:171
#: b3b302bad9154eb6a44eeb6c6e438566
msgid "Move your mouse over different variables and objects in the code. You will see the current values of many or the items."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:173
#: 992e82bd7ca84ca68278029de69034e9
msgid "Press F5 and Mission Planner will continue loading."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:175
#: efd0da40bda144b0bb045e61bb10b601
msgid "Further details on editing and debugging are left to the user."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:178
#: 44f1a60c03d94e9cae945f967d1c8995
msgid "Using your modified Mission Planner"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:180
#: 64020df16815441a933679b2db0c86be
msgid "If you make changes to Mission Planner, you will probably want to make use of your version.  Here we will give you some preliminary information to do that. You can use your local compiled version but the compiled output files are located in different places in VS and some additional steps are required.  There are configuration files specific to your installation of Mission Planner that are not included in the Git hub download that are only provided in the Mission Planner installation package. You will need to copy these to the correct area in the folder you are using for the Visual Studio project. Here are the steps that will get you started."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:191
#: 07b35b8420d546988cacaac6beafb27e
msgid "**Use your modified complied version of Mission Planner at your own risk.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:193
#: cae2af614594475f9c3c428115aeca03
msgid "These steps assume VS is in the debug configuration.  [editors]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:194
#: 9f79b3cb12d745ddb4dc02b5cb892e58
msgid "Details when in Release mode could be added [/editors]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:195
#: c26ade5a403c466f911f30fcc0c60da1
msgid "In order for your VS version of MP to function with ArduPilot connected, you will need to copy several files from the folder where MP is installed (C:\\\\Program Files (x86)\\\\APM Planner  or C:\\\\Program Files\\\\APM Planner) to the folder where your VS project compiled output is located."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:201
#: 8c5681e6622547b1aab9f3c00d6982ec
msgid "Todo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:203
#: ecf4b82627ea4440a09613fb9bd23bd7
msgid "editors: This needs to be made more accurate which files are needed, why etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:205
#: 06f4c0aec09149b8ab282d0c137220d7
msgid "**Copy (don't move) all xml files** (I.E. files with the extension .xml) from the root folder of the MP installation (C:\\\\Program Files\\\\APM Planner)  **to the bin/Debug folder** in the folder where your Visual Studio Mission Planner solution is stored. (the Git hub clone folder). This will setup your compiled version to match the current configuration of your AutoPilot (copter versus plane, other options, etc)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:212
#: cbe2adb588d24a848beddeb7f5989a03
msgid "I.E, if you solution is in folder MPGitClone, then copy the .xml files to MPGitClone\\\\bin\\\\Debug.  Some will copy without notice, but some  will ask you if you want to replace the existing file. Replacing all seems to work but you should investigate further to be sure you can use MP for real life situations before you do so."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:217
#: a73425c3994b48b1b3f0d8ade9f6d5f2
msgid "If you build Mission Planner in Release mode, then the files should be copied to the bin/Release folder. This has not been tested at this time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:221
#: 0f4cd6e51cac4315a77750bde11cc40f
msgid "Here are some other tips:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:223
#: 387e6748576742099baaba1c9d546d1b
msgid "Location of Logs saved when using your version will be in the /bin/Debug or  bin/Release folder. This can be changed with Mission Planner 1.2.63 and later versions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:226
#: a2afadcdcc6441fb81a6fe38f3a741dd
msgid "If you want to make a shortcut to run your version of Mission Planner without running Visual Studio, create the shortcut to point to the program ArduPilotMegaPlanner10.exe in the bin/Debug or bin/Release sub folders."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:231
#: fff3595aefa34451adcf5914bc359d15
msgid "At this point your local version of MP should be working. You should be able to connect to your ArduPilot FCU, Flight Data including status should work, Configuration should bring up you ArduPilot parameters, Terminal should work including saving and browsing logs. Flight Planner should also work. As mentioned before, use your modified version at your own risk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:239
#: e3d240b70f434c0985dfefc04feaad74
msgid "Submitting your changes for inclusion in Master"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:241
#: 2aa646a27f0c4b07b9f31db15ebf9d19
msgid "Generally the advice is the same as for the ArduPilot flight code (:ref:`instructions here <submitting-patches-back-to-master>`) but here is a very short summary of the steps:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:245
#: 572a38f97e78405592574e93b2de240b
msgid "Sign up a member of `Git hub <https://github.com/>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:246
#: dc6d2e1d360a4e6695515c183a73fb92
msgid "Create a personal Fork of the Mission Planner by going to https://github.com/ArduPilot/MissionPlanner and click on Fork  (Upper right corner area)  This creates a copy (fork) of Mission Planner files in your Git Hub account."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:250
#: 0ad5b66d3ecb4cf4962c859bf13b4115
msgid "Clone your personal repo (created with the Fork above) to your PC"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:251
#: dcf5c34be92a4bf7a6b067cd125d8f9a
msgid "Create a new branch in your repo and commit your changes and push these back to GitHub (these will only go into your repo on GitHub)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:253
#: 549fb4a1521f4b3683e3f1f25a86db7e
msgid "Use the GitHub web page to create a Pull Request from your branch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-mission-planner.rst:255
#: a1b251b3d6eb4bee8c54a9ab9841d41e
msgid "The owner of Mission Planner (Michael Oborne) will receive an email notifying him of your Pull Request.  He will most likely review, provide feedback and if he accepts the commit it will be added to master."
msgstr ""
